ck-wifikiller (2.5.26-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * WPS: auto-retrieve PSK after PIN cracked. Pixie-Dust cracks the
    PIN but reaver 1.6.x does not return the WPA PSK, so the attack
    stalled with only the PIN. Now Reaver.get_psk_from_pin runs
    `reaver -p <pin>` first (reaver is already installed), then falls
    back to bully (original wifite2 path). Both paths have a wall-clock
    timeout (45s) so a stuck tool no longer blocks the main flow.
  * Reaver.parse_crack_result: catch all exceptions (not just
    KeyboardInterrupt) so a missing bully / stuck process no longer
    crashes the whole WPS attack. CrackResultWPS saved with psk=None
    if retrieval fails (PIN still preserved).
  * Bully.get_psk_from_pin: add timeout + check both stdout and stderr
    for the KEY line (version-dependent).

