ck-wifikiller (2.5.25-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * deauth: maximize packet volume to ensure clients are kicked.
    Scapy per-direction count raised 16->64 (directed) / 32->128
    (broadcast), matching aireplay-ng do_attack_deauth (64 directed /
    128 broadcast). Per-burst now 256 frames * 4 rounds = 1024 frames.
  * aireplay -0 count default 8 -> 64; all NIC profiles aireplay_count
    unified to 64. Scapy-success aireplay backup no longer capped at 16
    (uses full profile.aireplay_count).
  * WPA deauth: print newline after each directed/broadcast target so
    directed deauth lines are no longer overwritten by the following
    broadcast line (previously only "*broadcast*" was visible).
  * attack: raise initial target_wait 20s -> 45s; weak-signal / channel-
    switch APs need more time to reappear in airodump CSV.

 -- 传康Kk <1837620622@qq.com>  Tue, 28 Jul 2026 14:00:00 +0800

ck-wifikiller (2.5.24-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * WPA deauth: seed known clients from airodump scan before first
    burst. Previously self.clients was wiped after wait_for_target,
    discarding Client.station entries parsed from CSV — so the first
    deauth volley was broadcast-only. Modern phones/laptops ignore
    broadcast deauth and only respond to directed (unicast) deauth,
    so handshake capture often failed ("踢不下人"). Aligns with
    wifite2 which seeds self.clients before the deauth/listen loop.
  * Extracted AttackWPA._seed_clients (static) + regression tests.

